From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:16:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] S1-02: removed-types-inactive (L-43, L-57, L-51)

The removed transaction types are inactive whatever the milestone says:
isActivated() returns false for 1/0 legacy transfer, 1/3 legacy vote and
the three HTLC types 1/8, 1/9 and 1/10, instead of reading the
legacyTransfer, legacyVote and htlcEnabled flags. The 2/2 Solar vote is
active whatever legacyVote says. 1/4 was already hard-coded off and is not
touched. The handlers stay registered, so both pool admission and block
application reject the removed types as deactivated.

The Managers import is dropped from core/vote.ts and htlc-claim.ts, where
isActivated() was its only use.

Test: patches/tests/02-removed-types-inactive.test.js. With a milestone
that turns all three flags on, it fails on the unpatched build and passes
here.

Patch: 02
Ledger: L-43, L-57, L-51
Consensus: yes (config-dependent only)
